# Unit30
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit30核心词汇

volume/ˈvɑːljuːm/音量；体积/Turn down the volume, please.
voluntary/ˈvɑːlənteri/自愿的/Participation is voluntary.
vulnerable/ˈvʌlnərəbl/脆弱的/Children are vulnerable to disease.
wage/weɪdʒ/工资/He earns a decent wage.
wander/ˈwɑːndər/漫步/She wandered through the streets.
wealth/welθ/财富/Health is more important than wealth.
weapon/ˈwepən/武器/The country developed new weapons.
welfare/ˈwelfer/福利/The government increased welfare spending.
widespread/ˈwaɪdspred/广泛的/There is widespread support for the policy.
withdraw/wɪðˈdrɔː/撤退/He withdrew money from the bank.
witness/ˈwɪtnəs/目击者/The witness testified in court.
worthwhile/ˌwɜːrθˈwaɪl/值得的/It is a worthwhile investment.
yield/jiːld/产出；让步/The farm yields a good harvest.
absorb/əbˈzɔːrb/吸收/Plants absorb sunlight for energy.
acquisition/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/收购/The company announced a major acquisition.
aggregate/ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt/总计/The aggregate score was 3-1.
apparatus/ˌæpəˈrætəs/装置/The laboratory has modern apparatus.
appendix/əˈpendɪks/附录/See the appendix for details.
appliance/əˈplaɪəns/家用电器/The store sells appliances.
apprehend/ˌæprɪˈhend/逮捕/The police apprehended the suspect.
array/əˈreɪi/一系列/There is an array of options.
articulate/ɑːrˈtɪkjuleɪt/清晰表达/She articulated her ideas clearly.
aspire/əˈspaɪər/渴望/She aspires to become a doctor.
assault/əˈsɔːlt/袭击/He was charged with assault.
assembly/əˈsembli/集会/The assembly of the machine took hours.
assertion/əˈsɜːrʃn/断言/His assertion was supported by evidence.
asset/ˈæset/资产/Good employees are a valuable asset.
assimilate/əˈsɪmɪleɪt/同化/Immigrants often assimilate into local culture.
assumption/əˈsʌmpʃn/假设/Your assumption is not supported by facts.
asylum/əˈsaɪləm/庇护/He applied for political asylum.
authorize/ˈɔːθəraɪz/授权/Only the manager can authorize this.
autonomous/ɔːˈtɑːnəməs/自治的/The region became an autonomous state.
backdrop/ˈbækdrɑːp/背景/The mountains provided a beautiful backdrop.
bail/beɪl/保释/He was released on bail.
bankrupt/ˈbæŋkrʌpt/破产的/The company went bankrupt.
barely/ˈberli/几乎不/He barely passed the exam.
benchmark/ˈbentʃmɑːrk/基准/The test serves as a benchmark.
benefactor/ˈbenɪfæktər/捐助者/A wealthy benefactor donated the money.
bizarre/bɪˈzɑːr/奇怪的/He told a bizarre story.
blaze/bleɪz/火焰/The blaze destroyed the building.
bless/bles/祝福/She blessed her children.
blunt/blʌnt/钝的；直率的/He is known for his blunt honesty.
boast/boʊst/夸耀/He boasted about his achievements.
bold/boʊld/大胆的/It was a bold decision.
boom/buːm/繁荣/The city experienced an economic boom.
breakthrough/ˈbreɪkθruː/突破/Scientists made a major breakthrough.
broaden/ˈbrɔːdn/拓宽/Travel can broaden your horizons.
casualty/ˈkæʒuəlti/伤亡/There were no casualties.
census/ˈsensəs/人口普查/The census revealed a population increase.
certify/ˈsɜːrtɪfaɪ/证明/This document certifies your qualification.
